    {
      "chunkIndex": 3,
      "contentPreview": "RULE: do not trust a small compiler error count while ANY declaration-level error (CS0115, CS0534, and likely similar \u0027this member doesn\u0027t correctly implement/override its contract\u0027 diagnostics) is present in the same project. Fix that class of error first, rebuild, and only then read the error count as meaningful. This is the fourth or fifth build-diagnostics-integrity hazard found on this branch (alongside phantom LSP CS1061/CS1739 during renames, and Synology ghost files resurrecting deleted",
